{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat","id":1281991,"title":"Help me play a technocrat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-21T12:13:24-08:00","id":1281991,"title":"Help me play a technocrat","content":"I've not actually got a game to play in atm but I like creating characters, working out how/why their magick works and doing some background, rotes, etc.<br /> <br /> But Technocrats have me foxed. I can't get a handle on them. <br /> <br /> I've read a fair few of the sourcebooks, old and new. I know Satyros has talked about some of the writing being inconsistent on certain points across the editions and books so maybe thats it but I have the following issues and require some discussion to help me work through them.<br /> <br /> 1) Do technocrats understand that they are a special class of people because of their enlightenment and do they understand that this is the same as being awakened? If not, how do they understand a) the tradition mages that were once technocrats such as virtual adepts and SoE, b) the tradition mages they re-condition as union members and c) the similarity between the existence of mages and enlightened agents (i.e. they both have unique perspectives that allow them to do things other can't)? Why would the technocracy even kidnap and re-condition mages if they don't understand that enlightenment and awakening are the same thing?<br /> <br /> 2) Do technocrats realise that they are altering reality through a property of themselves or do they see it ALL as training and tech. If the latter, how to they rationalise the same tech doing diddly squat in the hands of non-enlightened agents? Especially something simple to operate. For instance, weapons are simple to operate, they need to be because you can't fuss around with them in the middle of a fire fight. How does a technocratic agent understand their plasma rifle or rail gun or whatever not working, ever, in the hands of a non-enlightened agent, even if they very carefully explained how to use it somewhere entirely safe like a shooting range. Doesn't work for the non-enlightened guy, works for the enlightened guy. And he can see that the non-enlightened guy isn't doing anything wrong. And this also applies to EVERY hypertech device that he has been issued with. <br /> <br /> 3) When we are designing technocrats, how advanced should we make the tech? Guide to the technocracy says they are about a century more advanced than mundane reality. Assume slightly less none since they lost so many labs in the avatar storm. But 50 to 90 years is a certainty. Should we be looking at plasma rifles and laser guns or is this too crude. Are we talking Iron man mk2 suits (the suit used for the majority of the first Ironman film) or the more advanced nanotech version from Avengers Infinity War? Certainly the higher the tech, the more cool technomagick we can do, but it also leaves a gap of tech too advanced for reality, like exo suits, but not close to the cutting edge. Is this still hyper tech? <br /> <br /> 4) What about the cool stuff the technocracy should have thats only 10 years ahead of the rest of us. This would be much more likely to be issued to field agents and much less likely to cause paradox. Its entirely believable to deploy such tech as mundane prototypes and be almost entirely co-incidental. Is there any mention of this kind of tech in the books?<br /> <br /> 5) Reality zones. Guide to the Technocracy explained this as removing the variables that makes tech do weird stuff, such as gravity for space stations. But this makes little sense since a space station can be easily given gravity by making it spin (and I'm sure they have artificial gravity too). Do technocrats understand that their coolest and most advanced tech works offworld because these places are in areas with more malleable laws of nature? Do they get why offworld labs work? Since they construct their own horizon realms, one must assume that they have some understanding, or is this limited only to the senior masters?<br /> <br /> 6) Slightly off topic, but some of these questions might apply to technomancers from other magical groups such as the VAs and SoE, but I think they are far less problematic there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I can tell I have to play a technocrat on one of two ways. Either they do understand that they are will workers and that they have chosen to work their abilities through a shared paradigm that is readily codifiable and explainable and will eventually be introduced to the masses. OR, they don't understand any of the meta-physicks and really believe its all just really great tech and advanced training and simply can't understand why that gizmo won't work for that other guy but works everytime for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T13:18:41-08:00","id":1282001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat#post1281991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Do technocrats understand that they are a special class of people because of their enlightenment and do they understand that this is the same as being awakened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and yes but not in the way you think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If not, how do they understand a) the tradition mages that were once technocrats such as virtual adepts and SoE, b) the tradition mages they re-condition as union members and c) the similarity between the existence of mages and enlightened agents (i.e. they both have unique perspectives that allow them to do things other can't)? Why would the technocracy even kidnap and re-condition mages if they don't understand that enlightenment and awakening are the same thing? </div> </div> </div>They believe that the Traditions use different (dangerous/unmutual) <i>methods</i>. They believe that the other mages are also geniuses that use fringe and untested properties of reality to do their stuff<br /> <br /> The Enligthement it's the same and Mystics are stupid (and dangerous) for not understanding they're Genius powered unconventional science. Meanwhile SoE and VA are dangerous (and stupid) because they use similarly untested and fringe sciences, and they should know better.<br /> <br /> And some Technocrats even realize that the methods aren't all that different after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Do technocrats realise that they are altering reality through a property of themselves or do they see it ALL as training and tech. </div> </div> </div>They believe in the Genius. &quot;Empowerment&quot;, &quot;Mass Empowerment&quot;, and all that.<br /> <br /> Training and tech are important to alter reality (and they do allow muggle to opperate Devices, and latter to incorporate these into The Paradigm to transforme them into mundane tech) but they DO realize that not everyone can just do what they can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the latter, how to they rationalise the same tech doing diddly squat in the hands of non-enlightened agents? </div> </div> </div>It's not the latter. They aren't geniuses, they don't *get* it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially something simple to operate. For instance, weapons are simple to operate, they need to be because you can't fuss around with them in the middle of a fire fight. How does a technocratic agent understand their plasma rifle or rail gun or whatever not working, ever, in the hands of a non-enlightened agent, even if they very carefully explained how to use it somewhere entirely safe like a shooting range. Doesn't work for the non-enlightened guy, works for the enlightened guy. And he can see that the non-enlightened guy isn't doing anything wrong. </div> </div> </div>If it's something that only a genius can use then it's not that simple. The &quot;responsive UI&quot; needs to be implemented as a Device, which can be used by everyone provided the &quot;right training&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this also applies to EVERY hypertech device that he has been issued with. </div> </div> </div>...It doesn't, Devices can be used by anyone with the right belief system (inculcated through that special &quot;training&quot; that Technocrats so cherish and that's basically brainwash). The instruments and Wonders that aren't Devices are experimental stuff that the unenligthened wouldn't understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) When we are designing technocrats, how advanced should we make the tech? Guide to the technocracy says they are about a century more advanced than mundane reality. Assume slightly less none since they lost so many labs in the avatar storm. But 50 to 90 years is a certainty. Should we be looking at plasma rifles and laser guns or is this too crude. Are we talking Iron man mk2 suits (the suit used for the majority of the first Ironman film) or the more advanced nanotech version from Avengers Infinity War? </div> </div> </div>Be creative, even in it's weakened state the Technocracy can afford a lot. Nanotech it's certainly plausible and it's mentioned in ItX Convention book, that's quite old.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly the higher the tech, the more cool technomagick we can do, but it also leaves a gap of tech too advanced for reality, like exo suits, but not close to the cutting edge. Is this still hyper tech? </div> </div> </div>Maybe, Hypertech it's defined in M20 as Practice. Hence if they're better than what's reasonably possible today then it's surely Hypertech, but doesn't need to be Wonders: A computer enhanced trough an Hypertech procedure counts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) What about the cool stuff the technocracy should have thats only 10 years ahead of the rest of us. This would be much more likely to be issued to field agents and much less likely to cause paradox. Its entirely believable to deploy such tech as mundane prototypes and be almost entirely co-incidental. Is there any mention of this kind of tech in the books? </div> </div> </div>Books are kind of old...but yeah: Some exo-suits and not-so-clumsy robots are mundane enough than they can be made Coincident as long as they don't do stuff beyond what normal heavy machinery or a mundane robot could do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) Reality zones. Guide to the Technocracy explained this as removing the variables that makes tech do weird stuff, such as gravity for space stations. But this makes little sense since a space station can be easily given gravity by making it spin (and I'm sure they have artificial gravity too). Do technocrats understand that their coolest and most advanced tech works offworld because these places are in areas with more malleable laws of nature? Do they get why offworld labs work? Since they construct their own horizon realms, one must assume that they have some understanding, or is this limited only to the senior masters? </div> </div> </div>Void Engineers do (Tychoidean Metaphysics). However, between the secretism of VE and the disinterest lots of Technocrats show for the Umbra this information isn't as widely known as one would think. Technocrats that that don't spend a lot of time out there and who never studied Dimencional Science may not understand this kind of stuff (and they just rationalize it as being a cleaner enviroment or something like that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Slightly off topic, but some of these questions might apply to technomancers from other magical groups such as the VAs and SoE, but I think they are far less problematic there. </div> </div> </div>They ARE more flexible, but not by such a long shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as I can tell I have to play a technocrat on one of two ways. Either they do understand that they are will workers and that they have chosen to work their abilities through a shared paradigm that is readily codifiable and explainable and will eventually be introduced to the masses. OR, they don't understand any of the meta-physicks and really believe its all just really great tech and advanced training and simply can't understand why that gizmo won't work for that other guy but works everytime for you. </div> </div> </div>The 2nd applies for un-enligthened Technocrats. Enligthened Technocrats understanding it's closer to the 1rst one, but many don't believe they're &quot;willworkers&quot; so much as operating through some hidden principles of reality that normal people can't understand nor apply unless they're &quot;dumbed out&quot;. That's why they're Geniuses and not Wizards, they *get* things other people won't and they *do* things other people can't but they're not opperating on a purely subjetive reality, they're opperating on a reality that normal people doesn't <i>understand</i>. Only some believe that they're willworkers shaping the consciousness of the Masses to construct a <i>different </i>reality - and even they usually don't believe they're doing this from <i>zero </i>(they tend to believe in the Earthly Foundations).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-21-2019, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T13:24:08-08:00","id":1282003,"title":"","content":"For the paradigm stuff, the books sadly contradict themselves at time, but the fact that Trad mages and Technocrats can be converted to the other side does mean they understand they\u2019re doing something along the same lines. My group always decided the Technocrats see rival mages as doing superstitious, outdated, and dangerous forms of Enlightened Science. It also explains how they can justify their own history of the Order of Reason being often one step removed from the Traditions during the earliest years of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> They\u2019ve just refined their understanding of the universe and have better technology, especially as they\u2019ve decided to remove even the idea of deities of any kind from their paradigm. It\u2019s not so much they sat around going what should be allowed and not be. Think of it more as they decided for good or for ill that humanity must control every aspect of the universe; that we\u2019re not to suffer at the whims of fate and gods. It\u2019s all probability that can be figured out with the right understanding and technology, while all these things we thought were gods and spirits are just alien entities manipulating humanity for their own nefarious ends. Humanity must be saved from their control to realize their true potential, even if some 'backwards' cultures need to 'educated'. A lot of this is subjective, but in the grander metaphysics of the WoD as a whole, spirits, spirit realms, and many other supernatural creatures do play a positive and necessary role in their universe. And this arrogance of trying to wipe them out and cut them off from earth and humanity is causing a lot of metaphysical damage. Falling to hubris is an age old tale of being a mage, no matter what they actually call their magick.<br /> <br /> Edit: Aleph explained it better than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-21-2019, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T06:40:57-08:00","id":1282130,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep is that the whole 'Magic (Science) is done through enlightenment (genius) and Will (understanding) is abstract theory even among the Traditions. Sure Traditionalists are taught that on some level they are all doing the same thing, but for most of them that's some theoretical stuff that doesn't really matter. For most of them, magic works based on the detailed principles of their own paradigm.<br /> <br /> That's even more the case for Technocrats. Yes, they are aware that whatever thy are doing is impossible for normal people. Yes they are aware that Reality Deviants are doing something similar which is why they can be converted. Some of them are even aware that what the masses believe has an affect on the world. None of that matters, though, when they are actually working on advanced cybernetics, or exotic particle physics, or hypereconomic models. To a Technocrat those all work on clear, understandable principles that are very real if not fully understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T10:02:32-08:00","id":1282145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282003#post1282003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the paradigm stuff, the books sadly contradict themselves at time, but the fact that Trad mages and Technocrats can be converted to the other side does mean they understand they\u2019re doing something along the same lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only can Mages switch to a different outlook, methods, and Paradigm ; they also get to keep some of their Sphere capabilities and knowledge. In one book it's written that after a considerable change / switching of Paradigm, it costs half the usual experience points to (re)learn Sphere levels under the new Paradigm in regard to Sphere levels already known before the change / switch. I guess sometimes it is easier than this. This should be a definite hint and evidence for Mages that, no matter the differences and methods, they are the same kind of a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T11:55:07-08:00","id":1282169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282145#post1282145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only can Mages switch to a different outlook, methods, and Paradigm ; they also get to keep some of their Sphere capabilities and knowledge. In one book it's written that after a considerable change / switching of Paradigm, it costs half the usual experience points to (re)learn Sphere levels under the new Paradigm in regard to Sphere levels already known before the change / switch. I guess sometimes it is easier than this. This should be a definite hint and evidence for Mages that, no matter the differences and methods, they are the same kind of a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that it is. Raising a sphere involves both the study of what your paradigm has to say about a domain and study of the domain itself. Changing paradigms largely undoes the former but it doesn't do much to the latter. A Mage who's spent years studying Forces is going to have a lot of knowledge about how they behave, even if he's changing his views about why they do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T14:56:54-08:00","id":1282200,"title":"","content":"A word of warning, don't get too lost in the weeds when it comes to hypertech, dimsci, and the other high-end, far-out applications of Technocratic methods and practices. That stuff is cool to talk about, sure, but it's the <i>minority</i> of Technocratic goodies...and a pretty small one to boot. The most advanced piece of tech most Technocrats -- <i>even Enlightened ones</i> -- work with on a day-to-day basis is a regular-ass smartphone, maybe a bit more powerful when it comes to memory, processing power, wireless bandwidth, or battery life, but a regular-ass smartphone nevertheless.<br /> <br /> Put a Technocrat of each of the five Conventions in a room, and ask them individually to define &quot;power suit&quot;. You're going to get the Iron Man stuff out of two of them, the Iterator and the Void Engineer. The other three are going to start talking about formal wear -- colors, cuts, styles, patterns, fabrics, brand, favorite tailors, and fashion trends in general. The conversation <i>might</i> drift to ideal cuts for concealing firearms, or concealed yet fashionable armored inserts, <i>if</i> either the NWO or Syndicate person is a field operative of some sort, but that leaves the Progenitor high and dry since their definition of &quot;suit up for field work&quot; is more often than not a biohazard suit. That's what they know, and what they work with on a daily basis; for at least two of the Conventions (NWO and Syndicate) a good business suit is one of the most fundamental Tools (capital-T, as in the basis for Technocratic Procedures) of their Convention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T20:10:41-08:00","id":1282246,"title":"","content":"What Theodrim said. Despite the propaganda, there isn't one Technocratic paradigm (in the 2e sense of the term); each Convention has its own (though they take efforts to keep their various philosophies and practices mostly compatible with each other). <br /> <br /> You've got three \u201chard science\u201d Conventions (Iteration X, the Progenitors, and the Void Engineers) with the former two hitting hypertech hard in their respective areas of interest (engineering and the Life Sciences, respectively) and the Void Engineers immersing themselves in hypertech that's based on \u201cexotic physics\u201d (laser swords, force fields and blasters, etc.). <br /> <br /> And you've got two \u201csoft science\u201d Conventions (NWO and the Syndicate) with the former's hypertech being primarily in the realm of surveillance and information technology and the latter staying away from hypertech entirely if they can manage it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T13:45:59-08:00","id":1282330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282246#post1282246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you've got two \u201csoft science\u201d Conventions (NWO and the Syndicate) with the former's hypertech being primarily in the realm of surveillance and information technology and the latter staying away from hypertech entirely if they can manage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Syndicate has their own brand of hypertech, but it's not anything near what is commonly understood as &quot;hypertech&quot; in conversations about the Technocracy in general. When it comes to them, you're talking things like artificially intelligent (sapient, even) trading algorithms, <i>literally</i> predictive (as in Time and Entropy) futures speculation, office space optimization in digital web 2.0 spaces, audiovisual devices that record and capitalize office morale, and the like.<br /> <br /> The motivational kitten poster in the office takes on a whole new life when the poster itself is made of reactive next-generation synthetic fibers that dynamically absorb and emit light in wavelengths that trigger miniature endorphin boosts, and it's placed in the exact spot on the wall down to the micrometer where employees' eyelines are recorded as converging on their way to their workstations at the start of the day, after meetings and lunch, and at the end of the workday, so that employees unconsciously associate their workday tasks with aforementioned endophin boosts which raises morale over time.<br /> <br /> <i>[In other words, the kitten poster is a Device with a built-in Mind 3 Procedure that triggers mild euphoria in those who look at it, and it's put in the office where employees look at it on their way in and out.]</i><br /> <br /> Or, when the office PA system is programmed and set to play infrasonic subliminal messages throughout the day informing employees that Ted in accounting is a nay-saying asshole who doesn't think the current office project will work, and that everyone should band together and work hard to prove Ted wrong, because fuck Ted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 01-23-2019, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T18:28:06-08:00","id":1282365,"title":"","content":"Moreover, Syndics don't need to understand the Hypertech in order to get it to work. (Although many Syndicate reps DO have a working surface knowledge of various sciences. They need to know what projects are worth funding, after all.).<br /> <br /> The Syndicate, first and foremost, believe in the power of Dosh. More specifically, in the idea that &quot;you get what you pay for&quot;. Hypertech designed and built by someone else works just fine for the Syndic, so long as they paid top dollar for it and have confidence that the money was well spent. And the Syndicate bankrolls the whole Technocratic Union, so they KNOW the tech is legit. As such, many of the tools available to other Technocrats can be placed in the Syndic's Enlightened portfolio, provided they take the time to learn how to operate them. (When you pay as much as the Syndicate does for tech, you don't walk into it blind).<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not like every NWO operative is an expert in science, either. Yet their agents can use gadgets just fine. Only part of the New World Order is a member of Q Division. It's presumed the agents just pay close attention when said Q Division personnel explain how the gadgets are used. Their confidence in the efficacy of Union technology bridges the gap from there. Why should the Syndicate be any different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T05:40:42-08:00","id":1282415,"title":"","content":"Fair points. That said, one thing about the Syndicate is that their members take pride in achieving their ends using commercially available technology, with most of their Procedures leaning towards the Coincidental and utilizing obscure \u201cadvanced features\u201d of otherwise mundane goods and services. It is because of this emphasis on subtlety that others sometimes question whether they're even Awakened \u2014 though, to be fair, those who question a Syndic's Genius generally end up regretting it. <br /> <br /> In this regard, the Syndicate and the Void Engineers are polar opposites, with the latter regularly using hypertech that's not even on the Time Table at this point, and may never be. They only \u201cget away with it\u201d because their operations are mostly off-world, far away from the Masses; and even when they're on Earth, they tend to be restricted to remote locations. Ironically, in M20 terms, the hypertech of the Void Engineers is stuff that's likely to fail in Technocratic Reality Zones. It's still very definitely Technology; but it's based on principles that have not (yet?) been accepted by Earth's cutting-edge science. <br /> <br /> The main difference between the Void Engineers and the Society of Ether is that the former are still very much dedicated to the ultimate goal of One Truth, One Reality, while the core goal of the Society of Ether is to expand the Consensus until Everything is True, even contradictory things. <i>That</i> dispute is what was really at the heart of the split that drove the Electrodyne Engineers out of the Union: the bit about the Lumineferous Ether was merely the trigger that pushed them over the edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T12:58:17-08:00","id":1282486,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> mentioned, Technocrats generally see what they do as exploiting hidden principles of reality. Put another way, their relationship with Instruments is inverted from the traditional mage: where a regular mage sees Instruments as a way of channeling an innate ability to willwork (as represented by the Arete trait), a Technocrat sees the ability to \u201cchange the world\u201d as residing in the Instruments, and being coaxed out and directed by the Scientist\u2019s Enlightenment. In both cases, you need both the Instruments and the Arete/Enlightenment; but the perceived relationship between the two is very different. <br /> <br /> This has a couple of game system effects: first, Technocrats don\u2019t ever get to surpass their Instruments. Since they view their Science as being fundamentally rooted in their Instruments, being able to discard them and perform Science through force of will is sheer nonsense. Conversely, the fact that Science is <i>not</i> intensely personal and drawn from within means that Technocrats have an edge when it comes to making Wonders: in particular, mages who craft Talismans or Grimoires have to invest Willpower and personal Quintessence into the very act of doing so, above and beyond whatever Quintessence needs to be incorporated into the resulting Wonder; Technocrats who create Devices or Principiae (the techno counterparts to Talismans and Grimoires) can get around that requirement, as long as they have the proper facilities. <br /> <br /> And remember that \u201cInstrument\u201d does not necessarily mean \u201ca physical object\u201d: Instruments also include appropriate activities. And even those Instruments that <i>are</i> physical objects need to be activated in an appropriate manner. To a Technocrat, those activities are what make up their Practices, which are conceptual frameworks for how activities influence the world \u2014 as opposed to the mystics, for whom a Practice is all about how to focus one\u2019s Arete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-24-2019, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T15:49:14-08:00","id":1282535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282486#post1282486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to consider: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> mentioned, Technocrats generally see what they do as exploiting hidden principles of reality...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't even necessarily say &quot;hidden&quot; so much as &quot;heretofore undiscovered, misunderstood, misapplied, and/or not yet taken to the realm of practicum&quot;, as filtered through the lens of the Enlightened Anthropic Principle. &quot;Hidden&quot; has a certain connotation, that theories with little if any relation to the Consensus as-such can germinate and find widespread acceptance out of nothing, which <i>really</i> isn't the Technocratic MO; expanding, revising, even falsifying with evidence and replacing wholesale, theories that already exist, and creating new practical applications for existing, revised, and new theories, <i>is</i>. You don't go straight from &quot;Lo! Thor battles the ettins yon! Rejoice for Friend of Man has come to Midgard to stand for kith and kin!&quot; to &quot;hold on, let me set Pikachu as my buddy so he can get experience while we walk&quot; overnight, even though either way electricity's the topic of conversation.<br /> <br /> You can get into some real chicken-or-the-egg arguments when it comes to phenomena such as the Higgs boson and whether it <i>actually</i> existed prior to the introduction of quantum mechanics to the Consensus, but for what it's worth it exists <i>now</i>; while the &quot;discovery&quot; of it doesn't do much more than vindicate the Standard Model which has been dominant for decades, you can be certain Technocrats enamored with quantum mechanics are salivating at the opportunity of introducing technologies capable of Higgs field manipulation to the Masses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 01-24-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T02:00:26-08:00","id":1282604,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the Technocratic position is that the Higgs Boson has always existed. The Traditions' position is that the Higgs Boson is a figment of the Technocratic paradigm: that is, proving its existence depends on using Technocratic Instruments to detect it; and as such, the resulting \u201cproof\u201d is suspect and possibly the result of confirmation bias. <br /> <br /> I've said it before: if you need instruments to detect something, it arguably isn't real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-25-2019, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:20:38-08:00","id":1282643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282604#post1282604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, the Technocratic position is that the Higgs Boston has always existed. The Traditions' position is that the Higgs Boston is a figment of the Technocratic paradigm: that is, proving its existence depends on using Technocratic Instruments to detect it; and as such, the resulting \u201cproof\u201d is suspect and possibly the result of confirmation bias.<br /> <br /> I've said it before: if you need instruments to detect something, it arguably isn't real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merely pointing it out and deliberately shying from further discussion on the topic to avoid derailment, but the most interesting implication of that line of thought is the potential for near-infinite recursion. Did the potential for electricity's many contemporary uses <i>always</i> exist, or was it something codified largely by the Voltarian Order and NPG before it? We can pretty well bank that lightning and thunder have always existed, but what was it before the codification of Forces as such (either as the contemporary Sphere, or expression of a Pillar)? After all, in the <i>big</i> picture of all human history and prehistory, secularized will-work that in turn is the basis for concepts such as Forces itself*, is honestly a pretty new concept, dating back <i>maybe</i> as far as classical antiquity.<br /> <br /> <i>[By this I mean discrete, identifiable phenomena that are the result or cause of interaction between objects, signifying or being themselves instruments of change in the observable world over time. These phenomena being innate properties of the world itself, which can in turn be observed to determine how objects interact and how said phenomena effect change, as opposed to derivative of higher beings such as gods or spirits which would be in turn the source of all causation in the universe.]</i><br /> <br /> Hell, that brings us to the biggest chicken-or-the-egg question relevant to WoD metaphysics of all time: what came first, the thunder or the thunder god?<br /> <br /> Or, changing tact, did layers of the Umbra such as the Astral plane <i>always</i> exist, or did early mages exploit the concept of dreams to birth the Astral plane? Qaf is actually a <i>cleaner</i> example, considering it actually disappeared from the Tellurian to later be reconstructed as the Digital Web, but are we to take from that it was <i>always</i> an artificial space, was it originally a physical space to which supernatural properties related to the practice of Connection and Correspondence were later attributed by proto-Batini, or was it <i>always</i> a place of metaphysical import long before mages learned to exploit it?<br /> <br /> And, if Qaf is <b><i>the</i></b> Correspondence Point, why and how the actual fuck is the Shade Realm of Correspondence not just connected to <i>another entirely different planet</i> (that was discovered to <i>be</i> a planet two thousand years ago), but these two locations are sufficiently unconnected the <i>Batini</i> didn't even find the fuckin' place until the 16th Century? I don't intend to go reductio ad absurdum on this, but I bring this up specifically to point out and remind everyone how straight-up <i>weird</i> MtAs metaphysics really gets.<br /> <br /> All the same, ultimately my point is the Technocracy doesn't hold a monopoly on using their capacity for Will-work to create, in essence, self-fulfilling prophecies born of otherwise unfalsifiable notions about the world. They're just the latest, biggest, group to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T10:02:03-08:00","id":1282662,"title":"","content":"Those are all very good arguments for why the <i>Traditions</i>' view of a fundamentally subjective universe, where everything is created by human observation, is suspect. Again, the <i>Technocratic</i> view on the Higgs Boson (and similar phenomena, like the virus and bacteria of germ theory) is that it has always existed, and has only recently been discovered. <br /> <br /> That said, the Traditions' view is that Patterns are real, even if things like the Higgs Field and germs are merely how they manifest in one's chosen Focus. A Progenitor who examines a patient's Life Pattern will find cells at work, including an immune system that fights off various germs (which are their Focus' manifestation of maladies in the Life Pattern); a Hermetic examining the same patient's Life Pattern will encounter an imbalance of Humours causing the malady. Same Pattern, different interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T10:13:18-08:00","id":1282666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282643#post1282643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Merely pointing it out and deliberately shying from further discussion on the topic to avoid derailment, but the most interesting implication of that line of thought is the potential for near-infinite recursion. Did the potential for electricity's many contemporary uses <i>always</i> exist, or was it something codified largely by the Voltarian Order and NPG before it? We can pretty well bank that lightning and thunder have always existed, but what was it before the codification of Forces as such (either as the contemporary Sphere, or expression of a Pillar)? After all, in the <i>big</i> picture of all human history and prehistory, secularized will-work that in turn is the basis for concepts such as Forces itself*, is honestly a pretty new concept, dating back <i>maybe</i> as far as classical antiquity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, seriously, you shouldn't invoke half of the ceremony to summon me and then leave me hanging. That's very rude. But yeah, I'll refrain from any actual argument about whether things did or did not exist. An actual historical note, though. One of the moments that kickstarted investigation into electricity was the invention of the barometer. Not just because monitoring air pressure is useful to the study but because they started noticing occasional discharges within the devices. That was one of the first points in history that something akin to lightning was seen in a way that could be investigated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, that brings us to the biggest chicken-or-the-egg question relevant to WoD metaphysics of all time: what came first, the thunder or the thunder god? </div> </div> </div>A third possibility: they are inextricably linked as part of the same phenomenon, like the two sides of a magnet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, if Qaf is <b><i>the</i></b> Correspondence Point, why and how the actual fuck is the Shade Realm of Correspondence not just connected to <i>another entirely different planet</i> (that was discovered to <i>be</i> a planet two thousand years ago), but these two locations are sufficiently unconnected the <i>Batini</i> didn't even find the fuckin' place until the 16th Century? I don't intend to go reductio ad absurdum on this, but I bring this up specifically to point out and remind everyone how straight-up <i>weird</i> MtAs metaphysics really gets.<br /> <br /> All the same, ultimately my point is the Technocracy doesn't hold a monopoly on using their capacity for Will-work to create, in essence, self-fulfilling prophecies born of otherwise unfalsifiable notions about the world. They're just the latest, biggest, group to do it. </div> </div> </div>That's a lot to unpack so I won't risk derailing the thread by doing much of it here, but two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Qaf isn't the correspondence point. At best it was the location of it but I've only ever read that in the White Wolf Wiki. I also think the VAs would protest that. Their view of the correspondence point was a hypothetical mathematical point that shares a location with all other point. It's very much a computer programmer idea, if all points are the same point then the only difficulty of reaching something far away is addressing.<br /> <br /> 2) The strange thing isn't that there's a Shade Realm of Correspondence linked to a planet, the strange thing is that there's are Shade and Shard Realms of Correspondence at all. The spheres were just a common language the Traditions developed, they aren't the fundamental structure of Magic. My best explanation is that there's a lot of crazy stuff out there and Mages are just more likely to find the stuff that relates to the way they think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282604#post1282604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, the Technocratic position is that the Higgs Boson has always existed. The Traditions' position is that the Higgs Boston is a figment of the Technocratic paradigm: that is, proving its existence depends on using Technocratic Instruments to detect it; and as such, the resulting \u201cproof\u201d is suspect and possibly the result of confirmation bias.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know full well that was autocorrect in action, but I now have the idea of a particle flying through the quantum foam shouting, &quot;This isa wicked good fawce!&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: I can't believe it took me four days to realize that it singing &quot;More than a feeling&quot; would have been a better reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-28-2019, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T09:12:55-08:00","id":1283282,"title":"","content":"Returning to the conflict between &quot;We are exploring and exploiting the fundamental rules of reality&quot; and &quot;We are defining the rules by affecting the consensus:&quot;<br /> <br /> Part of the issue here is that we assume that the former is just a detailed and concrete explanation of the Technocrats' belief in science and the latter is a high level set of goals. Of course those two seem to be in conflict then.<br /> <br /> Instead it is more likely that the Technocrats are exploring and exploiting much more fundamental, complicated, and counterintuitive set of rules behind reality (much like Quantum Mechanics) that changes its behavior based on observations (much like Quantum Mechanics in popular science fiction) and can exhibit multiple different forms of emergent behaviors depending on circumstances. They don't fully understand these Quantum Metamechanics, but believe they are understandable. Furthermore they do think they can change the way they manifest in the world by changing how they are observed (that is, what the consensus expects). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T11:05:01-08:00","id":1285607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282365#post1282365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, Syndics don't need to understand the Hypertech in order to get it to work. (Although many Syndicate reps DO have a working surface knowledge of various sciences. They need to know what projects are worth funding, after all.).<br /> <br /> The Syndicate, first and foremost, believe in the power of Dosh. More specifically, in the idea that &quot;you get what you pay for&quot;. Hypertech designed and built by someone else works just fine for the Syndic, so long as they paid top dollar for it and have confidence that the money was well spent. And the Syndicate bankrolls the whole Technocratic Union, so they KNOW the tech is legit. As such, many of the tools available to other Technocrats can be placed in the Syndic's Enlightened portfolio, provided they take the time to learn how to operate them. (When you pay as much as the Syndicate does for tech, you don't walk into it blind).<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not like every NWO operative is an expert in science, either. Yet their agents can use gadgets just fine. Only part of the New World Order is a member of Q Division. It's presumed the agents just pay close attention when said Q Division personnel explain how the gadgets are used. Their confidence in the efficacy of Union technology bridges the gap from there. Why should the Syndicate be any different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Technocrat in the New World Order is an expert in regard to psychology and/or sociology, whether it is in practice, theory, or both. The NWO is a Convention to a large extent relying on their almost wholly Coincidental Mind Procedures. These are researched and developed with techniques and in conditions that could be considered to be equivalent to Hypertech ; certainly it is Enlightened Science.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Syndicate has this Order of Reason \u2013 esque expertise as Foci, as well as borrowing technology and theories from other Conventions. Other than Hypereconomics, they lack Foci that could be called their own.<br /> I think the direction and presentation of the Enlightened Science Effects for the Syndicate is decidedly worse than this of the other Conventions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282415#post1282415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair points. That said, one thing about the Syndicate is that their members take pride in achieving their ends using commercially available technology, with most of their Procedures leaning towards the Coincidental and utilizing obscure \u201cadvanced features\u201d of otherwise mundane goods and services. It is because of this emphasis on subtlety that others sometimes question whether they're even Awakened \u2014 though, to be fair, those who question a Syndic's Genius generally end up regretting it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this should be a capability of Technocrats of all five of the Conventions in general. The only reason why this would be speciality of the Syndicate is because it fits this Convention characterfulness-wise, and I don't think this is a reason enough.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:40:48-08:00","id":1285642,"title":"","content":"I'll certainly admit that it is often harder to think up what the Syndicate are up to than any other convention, however I would hesitate before I'd turn all of the Mind effects over to the NWO. The Syndicate is the master of human systems. Not necessary psychology (though certainly some of that) or power structures, but of how the complex interactions of people work together in unexpected ways. I would also throw Time effects like Asimov's Psychohistory (mathematically predicting the general course of future history) and Entropy effects that cascade through chains of people firmly in their wheelhouse. For related reasons manipulation of chaotic systems (any system where small changes to the initial conditions can have dramatic changes on the outcome) like weather and traffic also fits with them.<br /> <br /> For the more physical systems, they are very infrastructure based. Much like the VAs their tech often piggybacks onto mundane tech and they are the faction I think of for effects like sending objects through the phone lines (well they were in the 90s anyways, now it's cell networks). They are also the faction I think of for seeding mundane technology with extras that can be activated by those who know how. That not only gives them more opportunity for using their subtle hypertech, it also gives them more opportunities for unconscious casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:31:48-08:00","id":1286023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1285642#post1285642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll certainly admit that it is often harder to think up what the Syndicate are up to than any other convention, however I would hesitate before I'd turn all of the Mind effects over to the NWO. The Syndicate is the master of human systems. Not necessary psychology (though certainly some of that) or power structures, but of how the complex interactions of people work together in unexpected ways. I would also throw Time effects like Asimov's Psychohistory (mathematically predicting the general course of future history) and Entropy effects that cascade through chains of people firmly in their wheelhouse. For related reasons manipulation of chaotic systems (any system where small changes to the initial conditions can have dramatic changes on the outcome) like weather and traffic also fits with them.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want the Syndicate to lose their speciality in the Mind Enlightened Science. I think it needs to be defined and elaborated upon to a great extent.<br /> Giving the Syndicate additional specialities in kinds of Enlightened Sicence - and their own Foci and methods to go with them, whether it would be theories and methods of thinking, or Enlightened Science technology - is also needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T17:10:59-08:00","id":1286049,"title":"","content":"We'll have to just agree to disagree, then; I have no problem with the Syndicate paradigm as it is, and I think that turning them into another group of hypertech specialists would be a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T15:16:55-08:00","id":1286864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1282145#post1282145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only can Mages switch to a different outlook, methods, and Paradigm ; they also get to keep some of their Sphere capabilities and knowledge. In one book it's written that after a considerable change / switching of Paradigm, it costs half the usual experience points to (re)learn Sphere levels under the new Paradigm in regard to Sphere levels already known before the change / switch. I guess sometimes it is easier than this. This should be a definite hint and evidence for Mages that, no matter the differences and methods, they are the same kind of a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I agree. I remember there was some funny stuff written in the &quot;Guide to the Technocracy&quot;, about how they didn't understand what the other mages were and didn't recognize they were the same thing. I thought it was really silly. So I prefer, as you said, they all know deep down they're the same thing, but they just do magick/enlightened science 'wrong'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T09:11:41-08:00","id":1288618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1286864#post1286864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah I agree. I remember there was some funny stuff written in the &quot;Guide to the Technocracy&quot;, about how they didn't understand what the other mages were and didn't recognize they were the same thing. I thought it was really silly. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it makes sense for some Technocrats to have such an outlook and attitude, as long as it isn't a definitive and unchangeable stance. Mystics can also have an attitude of reluctance or skepticism towards the Paradigms and viewpoints that other Mages have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-16-2019, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:11:58-08:00","id":1288730,"title":"","content":"My take on the approach of the Technocracy is to present it as the most common form that Quiet (specifically, Denial) takes among Technocrats: if you truly, honestly believe that Magick doesn't work, you're in Denial. <br /> <br /> Which then leads to my views about the role that Negation Men are likely to play with respect to the Union\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-16-2019, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T11:30:18-08:00","id":1288958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1288618#post1288618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it makes sense for some Technocrats to have such an outlook and attitude, as long as it isn't a definitive and unchangeable stance. Mystics can also have an attitude of reluctance or skepticism towards the Paradigms and viewpoints that other Mages have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I remember they never presented a nuetral stance or multiple takes. We're simply presented with this one hot take. It's another example of WW often lack of oversite of its freelancers and flawed approach with the unreliable narrator as their framing device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T16:16:47-08:00","id":1289347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281991-help-me-play-a-technocrat?p=1285642#post1285642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll certainly admit that it is often harder to think up what the Syndicate are up to than any other convention...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the best guiding light for the Syndicate in its current state (actually having a Convention book, and being greatly expounded upon in M20) is...to look backwards. Specifically, the <i>Swashbuckler's Handbook</i> for MtSC. Hypereconomics is <i>Ars Cupiditae</i> with a 21st Century, office chic, flavor. In fact, if I remember right the M20 core book straight-up calls Hypereconomics by that name in at least one point.<br /> <br /> That alone is why OPP did something I never thought possible -- unseat the Hermetic Order as my favorite MtAs splat, let alone with a <i>Convention</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T18:59:09-08:00","id":1289376,"title":"","content":"M20 lists the Art of Desire as one of the Practices, with Hypereconomics as a specialized variant of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:10:28-08:00","id":1289750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the latter, how to they rationalize the same tech doing diddly squat in the hands of non-enlightened agents? </div> </div> </div>I don't feel like this line was properly addressed. Technocratic devices <i>do </i>work in the hands of Extraordinary Citizens (the title for Non-Enlightened Agents). They are trained in the use of these tools, but cannot do all of the same sorts of things that Enlightened personnel can achieve with them. Most Technocratic devices are not merely part of the Focus but also fully functional Wonders. Eventually, these devices merge into the consensus and become commonplace items - just look at the wristbound computer from Technomancer's Toybox, and modern smartphones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}